---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base current="home">
  <h1>Half-Baked Tools</h1>
  <p class="lede">Small, open-source tools for everyday questions. Every tool shows its sources and its limits, and keeps improving as better evidence and data arrive.</p>
  <h2>Tools</h2>
  <ul class="tool-list">
    <li>
      <a class="card" href={`${base}tools/nutrient-planner/`}>
        <h3 style="margin-top:0">Nutrient planner <span class="tag">New</span></h3>
        <p class="muted" style="margin:0">Find a handful of everyday foods that together come close to UK, US or EU daily nutrient recommendations for your age and sex, or build your own day and see how it measures up, with charts for vitamins, minerals and amino acids.</p>
      </a>
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Why "half-baked"?</h2>
  <p>Because these tools are never finished. Data gets updated, methods get refined, and anyone can suggest improvements on GitHub. What doesn't change: claims come with sources, and limitations are stated plainly.</p>
</Base>
